# armour/man/leaf: leaf armour on the man (ARMOUR-M, wave 2 r1; the Sylvan's elven harness, STYLE_P2 25.2, 28.5, 29.10).
# Courses of big leaf-shaped plates in the metal slot: each leaf 4 px across, its broad top lit (step 3), a mid row and a
# 2 px pointed tip over the course below with a dark gap either side, the courses staggered by half a leaf; the shadow
# side a step down; one glint on the lit shoulder leaf; a smooth lit collar band; the leather belt kept. Until wave 2
# leaf fell back to leather's jerkin (doll_resolve's chain). The base and `armour.t2` views keep leather's mask in every
# key (the slim elven cut: no outline or fit change); leather's studs are not carried. Finish regions as leather's.
# Generated by ARMOUR-M tools/gen_leaf.py from leather.pxm; re-run, never hand-edit. Format: rpg/art/doll/doll.h.
use person
body man
role armour leaf
layer torso
anchor neck
keys torso
z 2

